    "narrative": "Our offensive engine today is anchored by **Josh Naylor** (75.57) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92), both of whom capitalize on high-upside matchups against favorable arms. **Josh Naylor** benefits from an exploitable 5.79 xERA from Imai, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** faces Fedde in a spot that maximizes his platoon advantage and premium batting order placement. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) rounds out our top tier; despite his lineup status being officially pending, his projection is heavily bolstered by a +10% park factor and an 11% boost against Pallante, making him a high-efficiency plug-and-play if confirmed in the middle of the order.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our speed-starters. **Corbin Carroll** (59.39) and **Brice Turang** (51.53) are both starting despite pedestrian scores relative to their typical output. We are effectively paying a \"speed tax\" to maintain our edge in stolen bases, accepting lower efficiency scores to keep their legs in the lineup. **James Wood** (68.73) remains our most complete start of the day; his leadoff role combined with a neutral matchup against Singer provides a perfect blend of volume and plate discipline. Conversely, **Trevor Story** (46.48) narrowly missed the final cut. While he offered a nice park boost, facing a high-caliber arm like Wheeler in a tough BvP environment pushed his utility score below our preferred threshold, and the risk of his elite hold-runner disadvantage against the opposing battery outweighed the potential for a mid-tier offensive showing.\n\nWe are monitoring the **Dalton Rushing** (56.49) and **Brice Turang** (51.53) situations closely, as both are awaiting official lineup confirmation. While **Travis Bazzana** (59.62) looks like a stable play against the hittable Ure\u00f1a, we must remain vigilant regarding the weather and any late defensive substitutions. The floor is currently set by **Cole Young** (46.57); should his order spot fall further than #9, we may reconsider his presence in the lineup to avoid burning a cap on a low-floor utility player. Overall, the squad is positioned to attack high-xERA starters while sacrificing some raw power upside to ensure our stolen base rate remains competitive.",
